  "solution": "Given: 7 + 3 – 24 ÷ 6 × 12 = 29\n\nBy checking options and changing signs accordingly,\n\n**(1) + and ×**\n\n**LHS = 7 × 3 – 24 ÷ 6 + 12 **\n\n**= **7 × 3 – 4 + 12 \n\n= 21 - 4 + 12 \n\n= 33 - 4\n\n= 29\n\nLHS = RHS\n\n(2) ÷ and × \n\nLHS = 7 + 3 – 24 × 6 ÷ 12\n\n= 7 + 3 - 24 × 0.5\n\n= 7 + 3 - 12 \n\n= 10 - 12 \n\n= - 2\n\n≠ 29\n\nLHS ≠ RHS\n\n(3) + and –\n\nLHS = 7 - 3 + 24 ÷ 6 × 12\n\n= 7 - 3 + 4 × 12\n\n= 7 - 3 + 48 \n\n= 55 - 3\n\n= 52\n\n≠ 29\n\nLHS ≠ RHS\n\n(4) × and –\n\nLHS = 7 + 3 × 24 ÷ 6 - 12\n\n= 7 + 3 × 4 - 12 \n\n= 7 + 12 - 12\n\n= 19 - 12\n\n= 7\n\n≠ 29\n\nLHS ≠ RHS\n\nHence, **+ and × **is the correct answer.",
